    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.35.2</title>
      <pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 04:22:02 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>23502</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.35.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><p><strong>Ducklings that died with a restart stop showing as running.</strong></p><ul><li>When a duck's session restarts, a duckling it had running ends with it. Squeak now shows that duckling as stopped instead of "1 duckling running" forever, and it leaves the bar after ten minutes like any finished one.</li><li>A duckling whose state is unknown shows how long it really ran, not "0s".</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.35.1</h4><p><strong>A tidier Pond list and image paste that always answers.</strong></p><ul><li>All · Shared · Not shared now lives in the filter menu next to Ponds instead of its own row. The filter icon darkens while a filter is on.</li><li>Pasting or dropping an image into a duck's chat or a new duck never silently does nothing: it attaches, or says under the box why it can't. Images copied from Finder, browsers and spreadsheets paste more reliably.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.35.0</h4><p><strong>People in your Ponds: invite by email, roles, and a Room that works while your Mac sleeps.</strong></p><ul><li>Invite people to a Pond by email as a Member or Viewer. They join from the email in their browser or on their own Mac; Invitations show at the top of the sidebar with Join and Decline.</li><li>People sheet: everyone in the Pond with their role and when they were last online. As the Owner you can change roles, remove someone, resend or withdraw an invite, or delete the Pond.</li><li>Members' new Tasks and Duck starts wait for your approval; approving edits and Stop stay yours.</li><li>Leave, Remove and Delete take effect at once. Posts stay in the Room marked "(left)".</li><li>The Room lives in Squeak Cloud, so Members can post and read while your Mac is asleep; your Mac catches up in order when it's back. Pictures travel encrypted.</li><li>One connection line per Pond: Live, Reconnecting… or Owner's Mac offline.</li><li>Starting a Duck opens it straight away while it's created.</li><li>A new Dashboard, and a Shared filter in the Pond list.</li><li>Shared Ponds start clean on this version: your Ponds are yours and local again until you invite people. Nothing in your folders or git changes.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
